node_modules/
out/
dist/
*.log
.vite/

# Build artefacts and stray files from tooling.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Stray files from tooling that wrote a Windows path as a filename.
C:*

# Never commit environment files.
.env
.env.*

# Zero-byte artefacts from a notification hook whose path was not quoted. Harmless, but they
# land in the repo root and would otherwise show up as untracked work on every merge.
C:Users*

# vibePilot's own memory, in vibePilot's own repo.
#
# In a *user's* project these files are committed deliberately — see `MACHINE_OWNED_PREFIX` in
# git/repo.ts — because versioned memory is worth having and the merge path handles it. This
# repo is different: it is published publicly, and everything under here is written by a model
# from whatever the conversation contained. Nothing personal gets to reach a public repo by
# accident, so here the folder simply stays out of git. Both arrangements work; this one is
# the one that cannot leak.
.vibepilot/
